<title>BELGIUM: EU says probes RWE Energie Thyssengas stake.</title>
<headline>EU says probes RWE Energie Thyssengas stake.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it was starting a preliminary review into the proposed acquisition by RWE Energie AG, a subsidiary of RWE AG, of a stake in Thyssengas GmbH from Bayernwerk AG.</p>
<p>Bayernwerk is controlled by Viag AG. Other shareholders in Thyssengas include Shell Petroleum NV and Esso AG.</p>
<p>The operation was notified to the Commission for clearance on October 10 under the European Union's merger regulation, the Commission said in a statement. The rules ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>The Commission has one month from the notification date to clear the deal or start an in-depth four-month probe. -- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
